Introduction

The Canonically Yours challenge from the Intigriti July 2026 CTF demonstrates a JSON Parser Differential vulnerability, also known as Duplicate-Key Confusion.
The application signs manifests based on one JSON interpretation while the publication service processes another, 
allowing an attacker to bypass namespace restrictions and access a protected package.
Root Cause

The vulnerability exists because the application processes the same JSON document differently across two backend services. 
The signing service validates the first occurrence of the duplicated `package` key, while the publication service uses the last occurrence.
This parser inconsistency allows an authorized manifest to be interpreted as a request for a restricted package.


