Security Impact

Parser differential vulnerabilities can lead to:

    Authorization Bypass
    Broken Access Control
    Sensitive Data Disclosure
    Business Logic Abuse

Mitigation

    Reject duplicate JSON keys.
    Use a canonical JSON parser.
    Validate permissions after parsing.
    Share the same parsed object across all backend services.

Conclusion

This challenge demonstrates how parser inconsistencies can create authorization bypasses even when cryptographic signing is implemented correctly. 
A single duplicated JSON key was enough to bypass namespace restrictions and access protected resources.
